ozz-arrays-of-none: hand an Extern no array of none

An Extern that saves or loads an array of structs takes the address of a
member of its first element: Float3Key and QuaternionKey's values, Float2's
x and its siblings in math_archive.cc and soa_math_archive.cc. An array of
none is often an empty span, whose data is null, so each of them accessed a
member through a null pointer: an animation of no tracks, which ozz's
builder makes from a raw animation of none, or a track of no keys, of any
value type but float.

internal::Array, through which MakeArray hands every array to its Extern,
calls none for an array of none. What an archive holds is unchanged.

Evidence: zozz's src/integration_test.zig saves and loads an animation of
no tracks and a track of no keys of each value type; under
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer upstream stops in Extern<Float3Key>::Save and
Extern<math::Float2>::Save with "member access within null pointer"
(measured, 2026-10-31).

diff --git a/libs/ozz/include/ozz/base/io/archive.h b/libs/ozz/include/ozz/base/io/archive.h
index cea04c8..e3bc733 100644
--- a/libs/ozz/include/ozz/base/io/archive.h
+++ b/libs/ozz/include/ozz/base/io/archive.h
@@ -352,14 +352,20 @@ struct Extern {
 
 // Wrapper for dynamic array serialization.
 // Must be used through ozz::io::MakeArray.
+// An array of none hands its Extern nothing: its data may be null, and an
+// Extern may name the members of its first element.
 namespace internal {
 template <typename _Ty>
 struct Array {
   OZZ_INLINE void Save(OArchive& _archive) const {
-    ozz::io::Extern<_Ty>::Save(_archive, array, count);
+    if (count != 0) {
+      ozz::io::Extern<_Ty>::Save(_archive, array, count);
+    }
   }
   OZZ_INLINE void Load(IArchive& _archive, uint32_t _version) const {
-    ozz::io::Extern<_Ty>::Load(_archive, array, count, _version);
+    if (count != 0) {
+      ozz::io::Extern<_Ty>::Load(_archive, array, count, _version);
+    }
   }
   _Ty* array;
   size_t count;
@@ -368,7 +374,9 @@ struct Array {
 template <typename _Ty>
 struct Array<const _Ty> {
   OZZ_INLINE void Save(OArchive& _archive) const {
-    ozz::io::Extern<_Ty>::Save(_archive, array, count);
+    if (count != 0) {
+      ozz::io::Extern<_Ty>::Save(_archive, array, count);
+    }
   }
   const _Ty* array;
   size_t count;
